 "intro": "What to say in an emergency and at the lost-property office, with the present perfect and the imperfect.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "socorro",
   "significado": "help!",
   "pron": "so-KO-rro",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "interjection",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You shout it when you need help now. The rr is strong: so-KO-rro.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cuidado",
   "significado": "careful, look out",
   "pron": "kwi-DA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "interjection",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It warns of danger: «¡cuidado!». With «con» it is «con cuidado».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "bomberos",
   "significado": "firefighters",
   "pron": "bom-BE-ros",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is almost always plural: «los bomberos». The emergency number is 112.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "ambulancia",
   "significado": "ambulance",
   "pron": "am-bu-LAN-thya",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You say «llamar a una ambulancia». The c sounds «th» in Spain.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "urgencias",
   "significado": "emergency department",
   "pron": "ur-HEN-thyas",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is used in the plural: «voy a urgencias». The g in «ur-gen» sounds h.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "accidente",
   "significado": "accident",
   "pron": "ak-thi-DEN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has two c's: the first sounds k and the second «th» in Spain: ak-thi-DEN-te.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "he perdido",
   "significado": "I have lost",
   "pron": "e per-DI-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is «he» + «perdido»: the present perfect. It is used for something recent that matters now.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "he olvidado",
   "significado": "I have forgotten, I have left behind",
   "pron": "e ol-bi-DA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is another perfect: «he olvidado el bolso». The h of «he» is silent.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "bolso",
   "significado": "handbag, bag",
   "pron": "BOL-so",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "In Spain it is «bolso»; in many Latin American countries, «cartera» or «bolsa».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cartera",
   "significado": "wallet",
   "pron": "kar-TE-ra",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "In Spain it is what you carry in your pocket. In parts of Latin America it is a handbag.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "móvil",
   "significado": "mobile phone",
   "pron": "MO-bil",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has an accent: MÓ-bil. In Latin America people usually say «celular».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "llavero",
   "significado": "keyring",
   "pron": "ya-BE-ro",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «llave». The ll sounds y: ya-BE-ro.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
