   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "In an emergency",
     "texto": [
      "To shout: **¡Socorro!** **¡Ayuda!** **¡Cuidado!** **¡Fuego!**\n\nTo ask a person for help with **usted**: **Llame a** una ambulancia or **a** los bomberos. In Spain, **112** is the emergency number.\n\nFor something that has just happened, Spain uses the **pretérito perfecto**: **Ha habido** un accidente. **He olvidado** el bolso. **He perdido** el pasaporte. Many Latin American countries prefer the indefinido: **hubo**, **olvidé**, **perdí**.\n\nTo **describe** the lost object, use the **imperfecto**: the bag **era** black and **llevaba** a blue keyring. At the lost-property office: **Quiero rellenar un formulario.**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Perfect for the recent, imperfect to describe",
     "texto": [
      "Two tenses, two jobs:\n\n- **Pretérito perfecto** (**he / has / ha** + participle): what has just happened or still matters. **He perdido** el bolso. **Ha habido** un accidente.\n- **Imperfecto** (**era, llevaba, tenía**): what something was like or what there was. El bolso **era** negro y **tenía** un llavero.\n\nThe participle is formed with **-ado** (hablar → hablado) or **-ido** (perder → perdido, olvidar → olvidado).\n\nTo ask for help with usted: **Llame a** una ambulancia. **Llamen a** los bomberos."
     ],
